WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:04.330
Thanks, guys, for helping out.

00:04.750 --> 00:08.210
Eiko, are you good to drive?

00:08.210 --> 00:09.380
Yeah, I'm fine!

00:09.960 --> 00:11.920
I gotta pull my weight!

00:12.380 --> 00:13.960
It's not fair!

00:14.630 --> 00:19.290
I went through all that pain, but you get to leave alive?!

00:19.460 --> 00:21.170
It's not fair!

00:21.290 --> 00:24.960
SUFFER AND DIE!

00:29.960 --> 00:30.790
That's on me.

00:30.920 --> 00:34.250
But don't think you get to rest in peace
after those stunts you pulled.

00:34.250 --> 00:34.960
Wait!

00:35.460 --> 00:40.250
For a little while, we were almost friends...

00:45.130 --> 00:47.420
Then I'll let you decide how to handle her.

00:55.880 --> 00:58.880
And so, with the help of our Graduate,

00:59.170 --> 01:05.330
we successfully concluded our investigation
of the S-Rank spirit in the F Tunnel.

01:07.500 --> 01:12.250
While we walk the world of the living,
the dead drift through the spirit world.

01:12.250 --> 01:17.000
These two worlds sometimes intersect,
allowing evil spirits to do harm to the living.

01:17.790 --> 01:24.920
This young girl is gathering dark power
to slay the spirit who took her loved one.

01:25.630 --> 01:30.130
The grudges of the dead,
used to pursue a grudge far greater...

03:01.670 --> 03:05.460
On the way back, we stopped by a temple

03:05.830 --> 03:10.380
and entrusted the fifty some-odd victims' spirits
to the priests.

03:10.790 --> 03:16.830
That left us with the thirty nearly-evil spirits
and one Graduate-tier spirit.

03:17.420 --> 03:21.380
This time, we didn't leave
the injured S Tunnel ghost behind.

03:22.130 --> 03:23.420
However...

03:23.420 --> 03:25.920
So, where should we hide that arm?

03:27.000 --> 03:28.880
I totally forgot about that.

03:29.290 --> 03:32.290
You know, I've actually got an idea.

03:32.420 --> 03:33.250
Really?

03:33.460 --> 03:36.500
Yeah. Can I tell you about it tomorrow, though?

03:36.750 --> 03:37.460
Okay.

03:37.460 --> 03:40.040
With that all said and done...

03:41.250 --> 03:42.750
<b>HOZUKI</b>

03:42.750 --> 03:44.420
...we got home safe and sound.

03:46.750 --> 03:49.540
Well, save for what had happened to me...

03:52.290 --> 03:53.210
Go rest.

03:53.460 --> 03:57.960
I could hardly turn down the offer, so I quietly accepted.

03:59.710 --> 04:01.630
Eiko, on the other hand...

04:06.290 --> 04:09.460
I always thought I liked scary stuff.

04:11.210 --> 04:15.540
But that was the first time,
I felt my life was truly in danger...

04:20.750 --> 04:22.960
I realized...

04:23.540 --> 04:27.500
I've been so careless, so reckless,
thinking it was all just fun and games.

04:28.500 --> 04:32.670
Is this how Kei-kun and Yayoi-chan
have felt this whole time?

04:34.250 --> 04:37.960
Do I still want to stay involved after all that?

04:39.080 --> 04:43.500
I want to help them, but thinking about it
makes me shudder with fear.

04:44.500 --> 04:48.750
I can't get what happened yesterday out of my head.

04:52.250 --> 04:54.250
What do I want to do?

04:57.000 --> 04:58.040
I know how to find out!

04:58.630 --> 04:59.750
I'm going on a walk!

05:03.500 --> 05:04.790
Can I come with you?

05:16.170 --> 05:18.830
I said it'd be a walk, but it's more than that...

05:18.960 --> 05:19.750
Eiko.

05:20.710 --> 05:21.920
Y-yeah?

05:28.880 --> 05:30.460
Let's move down a little.

05:30.830 --> 05:31.880
O-okay.

05:32.790 --> 05:34.790
<b>Den-en-toshi Line for Oshiage</b>

05:37.960 --> 05:41.580
It's nice to explore the city by train, isn't it?!

05:42.670 --> 05:47.420
Eiko, did you have a rough time at the tunnel?

05:49.500 --> 05:50.250
Yeah...

05:52.420 --> 05:57.130
If you ever get too scared to do anything,
you don't have to force yourself through it.

05:58.330 --> 06:03.080
I want my family to stay happy and healthy.

06:04.460 --> 06:05.460
Yayoi-chan...

06:07.630 --> 06:13.710
When Yayoi-chan's parents died
and she came to live with me, she was only seven.

06:17.420 --> 06:19.790
My first impression was that she was a little weird.

06:21.130 --> 06:22.920
She liked scary stories...

06:24.330 --> 06:26.080
and sweet treats, too.

06:26.380 --> 06:28.290
Somehow, we were always on the same wavelength.

06:28.790 --> 06:31.250
It wasn't long before she felt like family to me.

06:32.290 --> 06:37.040
I went along with ghost-loving Yayoi-chan
and ghost-sensing Kei-kun

06:37.330 --> 06:40.630
to support Kei-kun through the fear
that always followed him,

06:40.630 --> 06:44.130
and because I loved sharing that sensation with him.

06:45.040 --> 06:50.380
When I learned they were collecting spirits,
I was more than happy to help out.

06:51.130 --> 06:52.000
But now...

06:52.920 --> 06:54.880
I gotta pull my weight!

06:56.670 --> 07:01.330
Yayoi-chan... there's a question
I need to answer for myself.

07:02.130 --> 07:04.750
To do that, there's somewhere I want to visit.

07:05.750 --> 07:06.540
Then let's go.

07:08.880 --> 07:09.920
Thanks.

07:16.500 --> 07:18.580
That was a rough one.

07:19.540 --> 07:23.380
I'm sure Yayoi-chan's fine, but I dunno about Eiko...

07:24.170 --> 07:29.420
Up until recently I'd been trying
to get back into normal society...

07:31.040 --> 07:32.580
Spirits are naturally drawn to me.

07:33.170 --> 07:36.460
It's been three years since I got tangled up
with that spirit at the end of middle school.

07:38.080 --> 07:44.330
Because I got Eiko hurt, too, I was so afraid of hurting
anyone else that I didn't leave my room for years.

07:46.000 --> 07:48.330
<b>REIO UNIVERSITY</b>

07:46.000 --> 07:48.330
<b>REIO UNIVERSITY</b>

07:46.000 --> 07:48.330
<b>WELCOME ASSEMBLY</b>

07:47.330 --> 07:50.460
But with the help of everyone around me,
I got into college.

07:52.170 --> 07:53.880
<b>Private Tutor Square</b>

07:52.790 --> 07:55.710
I even got a part-time job.

07:58.540 --> 08:03.380
Then, I met Yayoi-chan.

08:06.130 --> 08:10.630
At first, I thought she was just some weird girl
way too into the supernatural,

08:11.920 --> 08:17.380
but then I learned she
was collecting spirits to build an army

08:17.670 --> 08:20.710
and defeat the evil entity that took her dead mother.

08:24.000 --> 08:31.500
When I learned we could defeat the spirit that cursed us
to free us both from its influence,

08:32.420 --> 08:36.000
I decided to accept
what fate had given me and fight back.

08:39.210 --> 08:44.250
Though we ended up picking a fight
not just with spirits, but with an actual god.

08:46.630 --> 08:51.580
Or get tangled up with dangerous spirits
who'd harm anyone, friend or foe...

08:52.920 --> 08:56.880
Just thinking about it leaves me exhausted,
but there's no turning back now.

08:58.380 --> 09:01.290
Still, I worry...

09:14.290 --> 09:15.250
<b>Yesterday was a lot.</b>

09:14.290 --> 09:15.250
<b>You okay?</b>

09:14.290 --> 09:15.250
<b>Don't push yourself, all right?</b>

09:15.250 --> 09:20.250
<b>Yesterday was a lot.</b>

09:15.250 --> 09:20.250
<b>You okay?</b>

09:15.250 --> 09:20.250
<b>Don't push yourself, all right?</b>

09:15.460 --> 09:18.000
Yesterday was a lot. You okay?

09:18.420 --> 09:20.080
Don't push yourself, all right?

09:20.630 --> 09:21.630
Keitaro?

09:22.460 --> 09:23.130
Yeah.

09:27.040 --> 09:28.540
<b>Next Stop: Otemachi</b>

09:45.880 --> 09:48.420
Eiko, I think I know where you're headed.

09:49.920 --> 09:50.580
Yeah.

09:51.580 --> 09:53.380
One of Tokyo's historic sites...

09:53.790 --> 09:56.290
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO'S</b>

09:53.790 --> 09:56.290
<b>GRAVE</b>

09:56.290 --> 10:00.000
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO'S</b>

09:56.290 --> 10:00.000
<b>GRAVE</b>

09:57.080 --> 09:59.080
Taira no Masakado's Grave.

10:10.170 --> 10:13.040
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO'S</b>

10:10.170 --> 10:13.040
<b>GRAVE</b>

10:14.130 --> 10:16.080
Taira no Masakado's Grave.

10:16.920 --> 10:19.290
Enshrined here is one of Japan's
three most vengeful spirits.

10:19.290 --> 10:23.330
This grave is one of the most famous haunted places
in the entire Kanto region.

10:24.170 --> 10:26.670
But why'd she come here now...?

10:27.380 --> 10:29.420
Have you come here before, Yayoi-chan?

10:29.790 --> 10:31.000
A while back.

10:31.290 --> 10:33.290
Then I'm sure you know the story,

10:33.580 --> 10:38.290
but just in case, I'll read the story
from this ghost-hunting site.

10:39.250 --> 10:45.960
Around 900 AD, a familial dispute led Masakado to rebel
against the Emperor.

10:46.170 --> 10:50.380
He united the Kanto region and declared
its independence, with him as its new emperor.

10:50.960 --> 10:54.960
The Emperor named him a traitor,
and two months later, he was killed.

10:55.290 --> 10:58.580
His head was brought to Kyoto and put on display,

10:58.920 --> 11:03.540
but before long, anger and hatred corrupted his soul,
and he became a vengeful spirit.

11:03.830 --> 11:08.540
His head flew towards Tokyo,
seeking out his body to continue his war,

11:09.540 --> 11:13.750
and this is where the head landed- or so the story goes.

11:10.080 --> 11:14.080
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO'S</b>

11:10.080 --> 11:14.080
<b>GRAVE</b>

11:14.750 --> 11:20.830
Some believe the famous samurai's grave imparts
good luck in any kind of "battle,"

11:21.130 --> 11:25.330
but the same grave is said
to be cursed and haunted, too.

11:26.210 --> 11:32.580
After the war, the occupying government
tried removing the grave during reconstruction,

11:33.000 --> 11:35.380
but when a frightening number of workers
died at the site,

11:36.540 --> 11:39.790
rumors began to swirl about the ghost
exacting its vengeance upon them,

11:39.790 --> 11:41.880
and the project was eventually halted.

11:43.000 --> 11:47.880
That's why now, even though Otemachi
is home to so many skyscrapers,

11:48.250 --> 11:50.630
this plot of land still houses the grave
of the great samurai.

11:51.460 --> 11:59.920
Some people say their shoulders hurt
and their head aches when they visit this spot.

12:00.290 --> 12:04.170
Eiko, you wanna explain how you headed out
on a walk to answer a question for yourself,

12:04.170 --> 12:07.000
only to go straight for one of Kanto's
most famous haunted graves?

12:07.580 --> 12:11.130
Look, I needed to come here to figure it out!

12:11.130 --> 12:11.920
Go on.

12:12.290 --> 12:18.130
So, when I was in middle school,
we went on a trip to see the imperial palace.

12:18.500 --> 12:20.080
And Kei-kun was like...

12:21.380 --> 12:23.080
Kei-kun, are you okay?

12:23.080 --> 12:25.080
Y-yeah, I'm fine...

12:28.290 --> 12:30.540
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO'S</b>

12:28.290 --> 12:30.540
<b>GRAVE</b>

12:31.750 --> 12:36.790
I still can't sense anything spiritual,
but I could tell it was a scary place from his reaction.

12:37.580 --> 12:41.290
And it was the first place that popped into my head
when I thought of someplace scary.

12:42.540 --> 12:46.500
If I couldn't walk all the way here
without fear stopping me in my tracks,

12:46.710 --> 12:49.460
then I'd stop coming with you to explore haunts.

12:50.580 --> 12:53.250
But I didn't stop walking.

12:53.630 --> 12:56.250
The faster my heart raced, the faster I moved towards it.

12:57.250 --> 13:03.290
I'm terrified out of my mind, but my curiosity,
my desire, to see the unseen, to know the unknown,

13:03.920 --> 13:07.250
to feel that intense feeling again,
drove me to keep going.

13:09.250 --> 13:11.250
Now I know for sure.

13:12.500 --> 13:15.380
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO</b>

13:12.500 --> 13:15.380
<b>GRAVE</b>

13:12.790 --> 13:14.830
This is who I am.

13:17.130 --> 13:21.380
Yaoi-chan, I'm going to keep coming with you
to explore haunted places.

13:24.000 --> 13:28.630
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO</b>

13:24.000 --> 13:28.630
<b>GRAVE</b>

13:24.170 --> 13:25.790
It must be in our blood.

13:25.790 --> 13:26.630
Huh?

13:26.630 --> 13:30.250
I'm tangling with the supernatural to get Mommy back,

13:31.250 --> 13:34.540
but there's something else motivating me, too.

13:36.000 --> 13:37.670
I'm just like you.

13:38.210 --> 13:41.080
Serious terror makes my heart race.

13:41.630 --> 13:43.830
I want to feel that chill run down my spine.

13:46.130 --> 13:48.460
Well, we'd better keep it up, then!

13:50.210 --> 13:54.080
So, Yayoi-chan, is this place actually that dangerous?

13:55.540 --> 13:59.790
Not even one of Japan's three most vengeful spirits
can win the battle against time.

14:00.250 --> 14:01.210
Really?

14:01.830 --> 14:04.540
I would've liked to see him in his prime.

14:06.580 --> 14:11.380
If we'd come here when he was in his prime,
what terror would we have felt?

14:07.670 --> 14:12.670
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO</b>

14:07.670 --> 14:12.670
<b>GRAVE</b>

14:15.630 --> 14:19.580
Wait, Yayoi-chan! I had another question for you!

14:17.210 --> 14:20.210
<b>TAIRA NO MASAKADO</b>

14:17.210 --> 14:20.210
<b>GRAVE</b>

14:24.210 --> 14:30.210
<b>Don't worry, we'll take care</b>

14:24.210 --> 14:30.210
<b>of hiding the talisman!</b>

14:24.210 --> 14:30.210
<b>You focus on resting!</b>

14:24.670 --> 14:30.040
Don't worry, we'll take care of hiding the talisman!
You focus on resting!

14:34.750 --> 14:42.040
Wow, it feels good knowing where I stand.
I've got my mind all made up.

14:42.460 --> 14:46.630
Okay! I'm back on the ghost hunt tomorrow morning!

14:46.830 --> 14:51.130
But to do that, I need to learn from what's happened.

14:51.830 --> 14:55.830
Wait, Yayoi-chan! I had another question for you!

14:56.420 --> 14:57.170
What is it?

14:57.170 --> 14:59.630
It's about the dolls, actually.

14:59.920 --> 15:04.170
What matters more for durability,
the spirit or the physical doll itself?

15:04.540 --> 15:06.580
The strength of the spirit.

15:06.750 --> 15:12.540
But repairing damage to the doll
can help the ghost recover from its injuries.

15:13.130 --> 15:14.500
With some exceptions, of course.

15:14.920 --> 15:17.210
Huh. Okay.

15:17.880 --> 15:20.130
<b>If the linked person is attacked by a spirit,</b>

15:17.880 --> 15:20.130
<b>the damage affects the proxy.</b>

15:21.210 --> 15:23.920
So, with that concept in mind,

15:24.380 --> 15:30.380
<b>If the linked person is attacked by a spirit, the damage affects the proxy.</b>

15:24.380 --> 15:30.380
<b>The proxy's durability is determined by the spirit's strength,</b>

15:24.380 --> 15:30.380
<b>but repairing the physical vessel can restore the spirit's strength.</b>

15:24.750 --> 15:27.880
if the container is made out of material

15:28.210 --> 15:30.380
that can restore its shape even after it's damaged,

15:30.670 --> 15:34.420
we could make a semi-permanent substitute
without worrying about the spirit's strength.

15:35.880 --> 15:39.630
So if I put this slime inside a hard person-shaped mold,

15:40.290 --> 15:44.130
it'll hold its humanoid shape
even if the slime itself takes damage.

15:44.130 --> 15:49.210
That would make it a doll that can repair itself indefinitely.

15:49.960 --> 15:51.750
Let's put my theory to the test.

15:52.210 --> 15:53.210
C'mon.

15:55.880 --> 15:57.580
You're happy to help out, right?

15:58.960 --> 16:00.000
Anna?

16:01.920 --> 16:05.580
There are so many more haunted places to explore.

16:06.670 --> 16:13.750
I need to make sure you never disappear on me, Anna.

16:15.330 --> 16:19.040
You're gonna be my best friend forever.

16:19.960 --> 16:22.630
Ugh, where am I, even?!

16:22.630 --> 16:25.790
How do I have the worst luck ever?!

16:25.960 --> 16:31.960
I took the wrong bus, my phone died,
and I bought way too many heavy souvenirs!

16:33.540 --> 16:38.080
Guess I was too excited
after my brother's memorial service was finally over...

16:43.170 --> 16:44.750
A shrine?

16:46.380 --> 16:49.250
Wait, I can just ask for directions!

16:49.250 --> 16:51.210
They might even have a map!

16:54.540 --> 16:57.500
My, what a surprise.

16:57.880 --> 17:01.040
That youngling got himself a whole shrine.

17:01.250 --> 17:05.250
<b>ABE NO SEIMEI</b>

17:01.630 --> 17:04.460
And quite the big one, too.

17:05.290 --> 17:08.630
Perhaps I should pester him a smidge.

17:25.750 --> 17:29.420
Now that seems far more entertaining!

17:37.630 --> 17:41.420
So, Eiko, you said you had an idea
for a place to hide the talisman.

17:41.630 --> 17:44.170
Right, I was going to tell you!

17:44.670 --> 17:46.540
Whereabouts are you thinking?

17:46.710 --> 17:48.290
Well, we buy ourselves a house!

17:50.250 --> 17:54.710
Wait, we can afford that?
Doesn't a house cost tens of millions of yen?

17:56.000 --> 17:58.920
You'd think so, but take a look at this!

17:58.080 --> 17:59.080
<b>BuyAbandonedProperty.web</b>

17:59.080 --> 18:02.080
<b>BuyAbandonedProperty.web</b>

17:59.170 --> 18:01.420
"Buy Abandoned Property.web"?

18:02.170 --> 18:06.670
It says it matches buyers
with people selling abandoned property.

18:07.040 --> 18:09.130
"The dollar store for home ownership"?

18:09.130 --> 18:13.330
Yup! You can buy a whole house for about a million yen!

18:13.540 --> 18:14.960
They're all old, of course.

18:15.330 --> 18:17.630
That's still a lot of money.

18:17.630 --> 18:20.670
Which I've got! I've been saving up here and there.

18:20.670 --> 18:22.330
Damn, Eiko.

18:23.960 --> 18:29.170
So anyways, we find ourselves a haunted house
and turn it into a Graduate dorm!

18:30.080 --> 18:31.630
A Graduate dorm?

18:31.880 --> 18:32.880
Yeah.

18:32.880 --> 18:38.460
From what I know, you didn't have that black rope
when you first got the Graduates,

18:38.460 --> 18:41.920
But if you add another layer on top of the other seals,

18:42.210 --> 18:44.540
that'll suppress more of their negative effects, yeah?

18:44.960 --> 18:45.290
Uh-huh.

18:45.630 --> 18:49.460
Then we don't have to keep them so far apart.

18:49.460 --> 18:53.460
We could put them all in one place!
It'll make it easy to grab them or manage them.

18:53.670 --> 18:57.920
Plus, no one will find out there's creepy stuff there
since the house is already creepy!

18:58.130 --> 19:00.710
It'll be even creepier than the cache in my room!

19:01.290 --> 19:04.210
That's that! I've got some chocolate to snack on!

19:04.210 --> 19:05.580
Milk, not dark!

19:06.130 --> 19:10.420
Let's find a place in Tokyo or a neighboring prefecture
that's in a powerful place...

19:10.790 --> 19:16.250
The worst Graduates will still cause a little trouble,
so somewhere away from people...

19:18.500 --> 19:19.460
This is it!

19:20.290 --> 19:22.500
This is way too perfect.

19:23.000 --> 19:24.750
He said we can come for a tour now!

19:24.750 --> 19:25.420
That was fast.

19:28.170 --> 19:31.420
This "dragon vein" of energy flows from Mt. Fuji

19:30.580 --> 19:33.960
<b>Mitsumine Shrine</b>

19:31.420 --> 19:33.170
to the powerful Mitsumine Shrine,

19:33.250 --> 19:35.250
then to the imperial palace.

19:35.630 --> 19:38.380
<b>Imperial Palace</b>

19:35.630 --> 19:38.380
<b>Mitsumine Shrine</b>

19:35.630 --> 19:38.380
<b>Mt. Fuji</b>

19:35.670 --> 19:37.500
The house sits right on top of it.

19:38.380 --> 19:40.630
It's in a fairly deserted area,

19:41.000 --> 19:43.630
and just look at the selling price.

19:42.500 --> 19:44.080
<b>PRICE: 100 YEN</b>

19:44.460 --> 19:46.750
<b>*Stigmatized Property</b>

19:44.500 --> 19:46.330
It checks off all the boxes.

19:46.750 --> 19:47.920
And it's stigmatized property!

19:51.000 --> 19:51.670
Here.

19:52.790 --> 19:53.920
Are you the owner?

19:54.380 --> 19:58.460
I hate scary stuff, so I can't give you a tour,
but feel free to take a look inside.

19:58.460 --> 20:00.540
Honestly, I'd pass on it.

20:01.330 --> 20:04.330
I know it's the last thing I should tell you, but it's true.

20:04.960 --> 20:08.540
My dad was the original owner of the house,

20:08.960 --> 20:11.000
but I inherited it after he died.

20:11.630 --> 20:14.750
That's when I learned a bunch of horrifying shit.

20:14.750 --> 20:19.080
The dad and daughter renting the house
killed a bunch of people, then themselves.

20:20.460 --> 20:25.420
But if that was it, people would still
wanna buy the house. It gets worse, though.

20:26.250 --> 20:29.460
A female officer who searched the house
after the incident suddenly fell pregnant,

20:29.830 --> 20:35.420
and ten days later,
she gave birth to a baby with a giant head.

20:35.750 --> 20:38.290
It tore straight through her abdomen.

20:39.580 --> 20:42.290
Both of them died right after.

20:43.710 --> 20:46.330
Now the neighbors have started rumors about it,

20:46.580 --> 20:51.080
saying anyone who goes in will be cursed
to give birth to the murder victims' spirits.

20:51.670 --> 20:54.630
They call it the House of the Virgin Conception.

20:56.210 --> 21:01.000
Anyway, that's why I can't sell it,
and maintaining it is expensive as hell.

21:01.460 --> 21:04.130
If you still want to buy it, that makes my life easier,

21:04.460 --> 21:08.170
but I'd feel bad if something bad happened
to you two girls.

21:08.750 --> 21:13.290
It looks big enough, and it won't get many passers-by.

21:13.500 --> 21:18.080
W-we'll have to check the floors and walls
to make sure it's sturdy...

21:18.380 --> 21:21.460
Yeah, and catch any spirits hanging around.

21:22.040 --> 21:29.080
Once it's cleared out, then we'll have
the perfect property for our Graduate dorm.

21:31.080 --> 21:31.960
Okie-dokie.

21:32.080 --> 21:33.580
Let's go inspect the inside!

21:33.580 --> 21:36.960
Hello?! I told you all that to convince you not to!

21:37.130 --> 21:40.460
I'm leaving! Call me later for the keys!

21:43.330 --> 21:44.670
Inspection time.

21:45.040 --> 21:46.500
Let's ghooo...

21:46.500 --> 21:47.790
...ooost!

23:22.290 --> 23:28.000
They seem to have found the perfect house
to store their Graduates.

23:29.080 --> 23:40.130
But under its cursed roof lies unimaginable horrors,
desperate to repeat their deeds with new victims...
